格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"A typed runtime for long-lived, plugin-oriented Rust applications — lifecycle, exact service placement, typed events, deterministic cleanup, scopes, and isolation.","id":"gh:1335001737","install_available":false,"language":"Rust","name":"cordis-rs","slug":"dshbox/cordis-rs","topics":["cordis","deepseek-harness","dependency-injection","dsh-plugin","events","plugin-framework","port","rust"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"A typed runtime for long-lived, plugin-oriented Rust applications — lifecycle, exact service placeme"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"nt, typed events, deterministic cleanup, scopes, and isolation."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Cordis"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**English** | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Cordis is a typed runtime for long-lived, plugin-oriented Rust applications.\nIt gives application co"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"mponents one model for lifecycle, service dependencies,\ntyped events, resource cleanup, and explicit"},{"id":"p4s3","text":" isolation boundaries."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Cordis is useful when your program is more than a collection of short-lived\nfunction calls: plugins "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"can appear and disappear, services can become available\nor unavailable, configuration can change, an"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"d runtime resources must still be\ncleaned up deterministically."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"For applications, keep the historical package and import identity:"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"`cordis-rs` is now a thin application-facing facade over the v3 runtime contract.\nFramework and plug"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"in authors may depend on that contract directly:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Optional capabilities stay explicit semantic dependencies:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Cordis v3 requires Rust **1.88** or newer and uses Rust 2024 Edition."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"When upgrading from semantic `0.5` / facade `0.10`, update core, timer and loader\nrequirements toget"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"her to `0.6` and the facade to `0.11`. The facade re-exports\ncore types; mixing `0.5` and `0.6` core"},{"id":"p15s3","text":" types causes type mismatches. `0.6` is a\nbreaking pre-freeze line: public vocabularies expected to "},{"id":"p15s4","text":"grow are now\n`#[non_exhaustive]` (add wildcard arms and `..` patterns), Loader source rows are\nexten"},{"id":"p15s5","text":"sible and built with `PluginEntry::new` and `EntryGroup::new`, and two\ndocumented promises are narro"},{"id":"p15s6","text":"wed (creation progress after its commit, and the\nmeaning of lifecycle admission order;\nADR 0029).\nTh"},{"id":"p15s7","text":"e compatible-evolution rules, enum openness and auto-trait and operation-future\n`Send` promises are "},{"id":"p15s8","text":"recorded in\nADR 0042.\nFor step-by-step edits and earlier\nupgrades, see MIGRATION.md, the\ncore releas"},{"id":"p15s9","text":"e notes and the\nfacade release notes."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Migrating from 0.6.x"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"`cordis-rs 0.11.x` is the current application-facing v3 release line. The v3\narchitecture first ship"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"ped on the `0.7.x` line. The `0.6.x` implementation remains\non the `legacy/0.6` maintenance branch f"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"or\ncritical bug and security fixes. The v3 transition is intentionally breaking;\nsee `MIGRATION.md` "},{"id":"p17s4","text":"and `docs/v3-migration.md`."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## The mental model"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Five types carry most of the public model:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"- **`Context`** — a cheap immutable view into one Cordis Runtime.\n- **`Plugin`** — reusable behavior"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" with typed source configuration and runtime input.\n- **`FiberHandle`** — the lifecycle handle for o"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"ne admitted non-root Fiber.\n- **`Service`** — a typed, named capability published into an exact serv"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"ice realm.\n- **`Event`** — a typed runtime communication contract with explicit routing."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"A Plugin enters the Runtime through a deliberate boundary:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"`prepare()` runs before lifecycle admission. `spawn()` is the first operation\nallowed to create Runt"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"ime lifecycle state."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"The smallest complete flow is: define an Event, define a Plugin, prepare and\nspawn it, dispatch the "},{"id":"p25s2","text":"Event, then explicitly dispose the returned FiberHandle."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Run the repository's complete version with:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Lifecycle and convergence"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"A successful `Context::spawn()` returns a `FiberHandle` only after the new Fiber has\nsettled for the"},{"id":"p30s2","text":" current service snapshot. The stable result is normally:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"- **Active** — all required Services are available and `apply()` succeeded.\n- **Pending** — a requir"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"ed Service is currently unavailable; `apply()` has not run."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Requirements are declared with `InjectSpec`. They are lifecycle prerequisites,\nnot constructor injec"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"tion. When an exact required Service publication appears or\ndisappears, Cordis converges affected Fi"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"bers toward their new stable state."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"A `FiberHandle` exposes the main lifecycle operations:"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"- `ready()` waits for the current stable state.\n- `restart()` reapplies the current committed input "},{"id":"p34s2","text":"on the same Fiber.\n- `update(PreparedChange)` attempts a precommit-controlled typed input replacemen"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"t; a committed update keeps the same Fiber.\n- `era_swap(PreparedChange)` performs identity-breaking "},{"id":"p34s4","text":"replacement; a successful successor has a fresh Fiber identity.\n- `dispose()` ends the Fiber and run"},{"id":"p34s5","text":" successful successor has a fresh Fiber identity.\n- `dispose()` ends the Fiber and runs its cleanup."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"Dropping a `FiberHandle` does **not** dispose the Fiber. Lifecycle ownership is explicit."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"Resources registered through a Plugin's apply `Context` are owned by that apply\ngeneration. Listener"},{"id":"p36s2","text":" registrations, Service publications, tasks, effects, and\ntimer operations can therefore be cleaned "},{"id":"p36s3","text":"up with the generation instead of\nbeing manually threaded through application code."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## Application teardown"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"Cordis deliberately has no Runtime-wide shutdown API. Applications retain the\ndelivered `FiberHandle"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"`s they intend to end and call `dispose().await` during\nnormal shutdown. The demonstrated example Ha"},{"id":"p38s3","text":"rness records handles in spawn order\nand disposes them in reverse spawn order, attempt-all; that ord"},{"id":"p38s4","text":"ering is\napplication policy, not a hidden Fiber parent/child relation."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"Dropping a `FiberHandle` or `Context` is ordinary Rust Drop, not lifecycle teardown,\nand root-owned "},{"id":"p39s2","text":"registrations do not disappear merely because Context clones are\ndropped. See Application teardown f"},{"id":"p39s3","text":"or the\ncomplete demonstrated pattern, including repeated teardown, generation cleanup,\nand Loader ha"},{"id":"p39s4","text":"demonstrated pattern, including repeated teardown, generation cleanup,\nand Loader handoff ownership."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"## Services: exact placement, not fallback lookup"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"A Service is identified by its semantic Service name and resolved from one exact\nslot:"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"By default a Context uses the Runtime's default realm. Isolation changes the\nrealm selected for spec"},{"id":"p43s2","text":"t uses the Runtime's default realm. Isolation changes the\nrealm selected for specific Service names."},{"id":"p44s1","text":"To give one Service a fresh private slot:"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p46s1","text":"To isolate several Services, chain the operation:"},{"id":"p47s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
